<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:56:20Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Live: Up to 500 schools to shut in France as student protests continue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:039513d74d5379f72411df34d1f5cfb44af76fee558bbe66b8f8645b11f19eaf</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:56:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T05:15:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261005-live-up-to-500-schools-to-shut-in-france-as-student-protests-continue--e57e83b73f71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261005-live-up-to-500-schools-to-shut-in-france-as-student-protests-continue" /><summary type="html">Up to 500 schools are expected to close across France on Monday as student protests continue, according to the country's Education Minister Édouard Geffray. The protests over high teacher absence rates, overlong school days and dilapidated facilities began at a Paris school on September 17 but grew into a nationwide movement last week. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Rubio visits Iceland ‘to discuss security collaboration’ as US boosts Arctic presence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce49851c12ae71e7792fa494294a3d4db77e529bb047011b2cc43be12b84c093</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:56:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T01:20:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261005-rubio-visits-iceland-as-us-boosts-arctic-presence-after-greenland-security-pact--fbd4e46a038b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261005-rubio-visits-iceland-as-us-boosts-arctic-presence-after-greenland-security-pact" /><summary type="html">US Secretary of State Marco Rubio is set to travel to Iceland on Monday, two weeks after Washington sealed a security pact with Denmark and Greenland on the sidelines of the United Nations General Assembly. Rubio will meet with officials in Reykjavik "to discuss economic and security collaboration", according to a statement by the US State Department.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Brazil presidential election heads to runoff with Bolsonaro ahead of Lula</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d7491fc683e68c0b99eafdb8e602f0c1349401452c011259a86c7e71efcde53</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:56:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T00:18:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-brazil-presidential-election-runoff-bolsonaro-lula--792d040be18d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-brazil-presidential-election-runoff-bolsonaro-lula" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil presidential election heads to runoff as Bolsonaro leads Lula</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d32f158cf9835317b8560fc6d57297e3769d4c7c4089d2c1e7a8748741b1289c</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:56:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T00:16:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-brazil-presidential-election-runoff-bolsonaro-lula--792d040be18d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-brazil-presidential-election-runoff-bolsonaro-lula" /><summary type="html">Right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro pulled off a surprise first-place finish ahead of President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva in Sunday's election, which heads to a run-off vote on October 25 as neither clinched a majority.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Pacific leaders urge climate action as UN pre-COP talks open in Fiji</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be4dac8a44d9062ef14883a5e6d2bcce9f9422af8a2b028995f29e5f39bef388</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:56:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T23:21:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/environment/20261004-pacific-leaders-climate-action-un-pre-cop-talks-fiji--188efcdaa5e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/environment/20261004-pacific-leaders-climate-action-un-pre-cop-talks-fiji" /><summary type="html">Pacific leaders urged action on climate change as UN pre-COP talks opened in Fiji's Nadi on Monday, ahead of next month's COP31 summit in Turkey. Discussions in Fiji and Tuvalu will focus on limiting warming to 1.5C, improving access to climate finance and protecting oceans as rising seas threaten communities.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>US withdraws B-1 bombers from British military base RAF Fairford amid security concerns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd4697d2b306109b9119a3515fa7a0f189db9ba5fa42f93a5df798ee39fae6e6</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:56:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T22:50:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261004-us-bombers-raf-fairford-uk-pentagon--df59450487f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261004-us-bombers-raf-fairford-uk-pentagon" /><summary type="html">The Pentagon confirmed on Sunday that all US B-1 bombers deployed to Britain’s RAF Fairford had returned home following a security incident that prompted nearby evacuations. Police found no explosives after reports of suspicious activity at the base last Sunday. Five London-based British men arrested were subsequently released on bail.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Iran says no military solution to war as peace talks with US stall</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fb7c8b134e0dbff568bca50f3c2cb869ee26162a5b8ee98d1813dfd0feb735b</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:56:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T21:41:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-iran-us-military-middle-east-war-peace-talks--489f2da42d26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-iran-us-military-middle-east-war-peace-talks" /><summary type="html">Iran's diplomat said on Sunday there was no military solution to the US war against Iran as peace talks appeared stalled. Washington has scaled back attacks in favour of economic pressure, while Iran's attempted Hormuz blockade remains contentious. A UK maritime agency reported another tanker hit by an unidentified projectile.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>A Profile of Brazil's Potential President</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cbd297f85dbaa3fb95e7fff6b1cc21105b80ecf17f549863c5e988949e9dc4b</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T18:34:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261004-a-profile-of-brazil-s-potential-president--ddef5eefc576.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261004-a-profile-of-brazil-s-potential-president" /><summary type="html">France 24's Gavin Lee speaks to Brazil analyst Henrique Tavares Furtado about how Flavio Bolsonaro is pledging to reshape the country, and asks: who is the man behind the political persona?</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil heads to the polls for high-stakes election between Lula and Flavio Bolsonaro</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:581ede8955f914550d29232106bcac72b9ab89f44d96f200c1dc619ef46d42e1</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T16:38:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-heads-to-the-polls-for-high-stakes-election-between-lula-and-flavio-bolsonaro--00531a37ca37.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-heads-to-the-polls-for-high-stakes-election-between-lula-and-flavio-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">Brazilians began casting their votes on Sunday in a closely watch presidential election pitting incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva against right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro, son of former president Jair Bolsonaro. Nearly 160 million voters will also pick lawmakers, senators and governors in an election that will determine whether Latin America's biggest nation follows a regional swing to the right championed by US President Donald Trump. France24 International affairs commentator Douglas Herbert shares further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>Evenepoel snatches photo-finish win to clinch European road cycling crown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4a6b0a9fffcddf8fc9d598bdb5a604ac18b8accd7cbd1376655748f0c9946d8</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T16:28:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20261004-evenepoel-snatches-photo-finish-win-to-clinch-european-road-cycling-crown--7247e4e91bea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261004-evenepoel-snatches-photo-finish-win-to-clinch-european-road-cycling-crown" /><summary type="html">Belgium's Olympic road racing champion Remco Evenepoel took the European championship title on Sunday after outsprinting Italy's Giulio Ciccone in a tight photo finish, just weeks after narrowly missing out on the world championship crown.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Woman at centre of Cornell gang rape lawsuit targeted with threats, lawyer says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46ab50eabbf070d89d6c649626c9f48da213b5109ff8ba5c3c9734e81c83cd43</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T16:25:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261004-woman-at-center-of-cornell-gang-rape-allegations-targeted-with-threats-jane-doe--374a939685ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261004-woman-at-center-of-cornell-gang-rape-allegations-targeted-with-threats-jane-doe" /><summary type="html">The woman who alleged that she was drugged and raped by seven male students at a Cornell University fraternity house has been the target of threats, her lawyer told CNN on Sunday. Cornell's president earlier voiced support for an external review of the Ivy League institution facing widespread outcry over its handling of the case.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>German Chancellor in Kyiv: "Ukraine will need our support"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f23f74082cfbd4b77d02dee6e7e927f557e58f6155f6b810aa115c0c8df9064</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T14:37:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/german-chancellor-in-kyiv-ukraine-will-need-our-support--5af0a63778a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/german-chancellor-in-kyiv-ukraine-will-need-our-support" /><summary type="html">German Chancellor Friedrich Merz visited Ukraine on Sunday to show solidarity after Russian attacks on Kyiv infrastructure, including three bridges. Last month, Germany’s foreign minister called for de-escalation during talks with his Russian counterpart at the UN, drawing criticism from Sergei Lavrov, who urged Berlin to stop arming Ukraine. On Saturday, Moscow called on foreign nationals and diplomats to leave Ukraine. Shirli Sitbon reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why I quit the movement shaping AI</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:305cf33c36ada0b87c097db80245db4198fc73f5abdfda36b04e2cbfe4a58a95</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T14:30:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/tech-24/20261004-why-i-quit-the-movement-shaping-ai--c7e4cd87dc53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/tech-24/20261004-why-i-quit-the-movement-shaping-ai" /><summary type="html">Artificial intelligence insiders are quitting their jobs, saying the technology could mean the end of humanity. Pope Leo in France warned of a “paradise of machines”. And the New York Times reported this week that one of AI firm Anthropic’s co-founders spent months lobbying religious thinkers on the possibility that AI could be conscious.</summary><category term="Tech 24" /></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Disaster averted on Flydubai flight, French school protests and Bangkok floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5992b155cb93fb18729fbeee20447bc4b6451592bcc546c23e018923e229da34</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T13:35:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-the-week-in-pictures-disaster-averted-flydubai-flight-french-school-protests-and-bangkok-fl--aacc58ef2e53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-the-week-in-pictures-disaster-averted-flydubai-flight-french-school-protests-and-bangkok-floods" /><summary type="html">From French highschoolers protesting to demand better learning conditions to a Flydubai flight diverted to Saudi Arabia after a flightcrew member's onboard attack and flooded streets in Bangkok, FRANCE 24 looks back at the week's most striking pictures.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil: Lula and Bolsonaro tied in polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b0e7debd97120e1273042accb22991ebb92613f74e7650b4b5752a92de23d34</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T13:19:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-lula-and-bolsonaro-tied-in-polls--985ac9bf96f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-lula-and-bolsonaro-tied-in-polls" /><summary type="html">Brazilians began casting their votes on Sunday in a closely watch presidential election pitting incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva against right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro, son of former president Jair Bolsonaro. Mara Nogueira, Senior Lecturer in Urban Geography at Birbeck, University of London, says the tight race reflects the consolidation of two political camps, with many Brazilians voting not out of support for a candidate, but to keep the other out of power. She points to the cost of living, religion and social media echo chambers as key factors shaping the vote, alongside a major banking scandal that has so far had limited impact on Flavio Bolsonaro’s campaign.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lula de Silva: 80-year-old incumbent Brazilian president seeks 4th term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15749e1307fa5b918fe85e7d3b8780d64c523ca9d5a5155eeda34302c703bd3a</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T13:17:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lula-de-silva-80-year-old-incumbent-brazilian-president-seeks-4th-term--6f4499fd648a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lula-de-silva-80-year-old-incumbent-brazilian-president-seeks-4th-term" /><summary type="html">Brazilians began casting their votes on Sunday in a closely watch presidential election pitting incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva against right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro, son of former president Jair Bolsonaro. Nearly 160 million voters will also pick lawmakers, senators and governors in an election that will determine whether Latin America's biggest nation follows a regional swing to the right championed by US President Donald Trump. France 24 correspondent Jan Onoszko tells us the latest from Rio de Janeiro.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen's government declares counter-offensive as Houthis cut vital route to besieged city</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d0f3678bad7f55288137d6c78ac146bb9c4d11972f877146c50798cb97889809</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T12:59:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-yemen-leader-announces-counter-offensive-as-houthis-cut-off-supply-route-besieged-city-taiz--d567521fb6d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-yemen-leader-announces-counter-offensive-as-houthis-cut-off-supply-route-besieged-city-taiz" /><summary type="html">The ​leader of ​Yemen's Saudi-backed government announced the beginning of a ​major ‌military ⁠operation against the Iran-backed Houthis ‌on Sunday aimed at ⁠recapturing territory under their control. The announcement came as Houthi forces cut off a vital supply route to the besieged government-held city of Taiz, according to several security sources.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Hundreds of schools to shut Monday as France braces for more student protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:804e8749072fcd42ec6eba1a0468486f947eae9fec422bc5909ac58b2009e887</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T12:50:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261004-up-to-500-french-schools-to-be-totally-or-partly-closed-monday-due-to-protests--c3c3dbff6b67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261004-up-to-500-french-schools-to-be-totally-or-partly-closed-monday-due-to-protests" /><summary type="html">France's education minister said lessons would be "totally or partly suspended" at up to 500 high schools on Monday after several days of sometimes violent protests against teacher shortages, dilapidated school buildings and overcrowding in classrooms. The minister said 24 schools had been "burned or ransacked" since the start of the protest movement.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Rwandan genocide suspect 'hunter' Dafroza Gauthier dies at 72</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e19a74ea628d0f848720402b3db3cf79d262b1aaf5261998c7fce986c50a4247</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T12:12:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261004-rwandan-genocide-hunter-dafroza-gauthier-dies-at-72--4acbb8946f0b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261004-rwandan-genocide-hunter-dafroza-gauthier-dies-at-72" /><summary type="html">For nearly 30 years, Dafroza Gauthier, along with her husband Alain, tracked down Rwandan refugees in France suspected of having participated in the Tutsi genocide. She died in Reims on Saturday after dedicating her life to bringing to justice those allegedly responsible for the 1994 massacre of more than 800,000 people.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>West Bank: Palestinians ‘harassed’ by settlers’ increasing use of drones</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf09886bfbbf48daebdcfe79f75c840cc38b8783a650d1882cf00785927e8680</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T12:01:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-occupied-west-bank-palestinians-harassed-settlers-drones--66a927f7344d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-occupied-west-bank-palestinians-harassed-settlers-drones" /><summary type="html">Palestinians and activists report an increased use of drones in the occupied West Bank, particularly by the army and settlers, to whom the government supplies the drones directly. The drones are used to intimidate, monitor, demolish and make daily life unbearable.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Lula and Bolsonaro face off in Brazil presidential race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a16c434fa1ebfbf776d10e975f6a0fff45207407b88e55020eb80c8068e54249</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T11:56:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lula-and-bolsonaro-face-off-in-brazil-presidential-race--d6b55874ce57.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lula-and-bolsonaro-face-off-in-brazil-presidential-race" /><summary type="html">Twelve candidates are on the ballot, but the presidential race is centred on two rivals: President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and Flavio Bolsonaro. Lula is seeking a fourth and final term, warning that Brazil’s sovereignty is at stake amid pressure from Donald Trump. Bolsonaro, meanwhile, has highlighted his ties to the White House, saying Brazil needs better deals with the US, including over its rare mineral resources. Nick Rushworth has more on the controversial senator. Dr Andrea Aruska de Souza Santos, Director of King's College Brazil Institute in London, shares further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>Cornell president breaks silence over alleged campus rape</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85f4a7e532201fa4b2ade27596b479cc6be2c897ca8118b563a00894375ab04f</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T11:53:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/cornell-president-breaks-silence-over-alleged-campus-rape--cdaa86cfffd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/cornell-president-breaks-silence-over-alleged-campus-rape" /><summary type="html">Cornell University remains at the centre of controversy over an alleged gang rape at a fraternity on campus, with the university president now breaking his silence. In an eight-minute video statement released Saturday night, Michael Kotlikoff called the allegations, made by a woman known as Jane Doe, deeply disturbing and said the university must do better. Shirli Sitbon has this report.</summary></entry><entry><title>Polls close in Brazil's high-stakes election pitting Lula against Flavio Bolsonaro</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:808b951dcfcfb9b6612572967baa9e422c352a3f53a243212bdb1bbe25e88ecd</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T11:17:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261004-brazilians-start-voting-in-tight-election-between-lula-and-flavio-bolsonaro--de08e320fb32.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261004-brazilians-start-voting-in-tight-election-between-lula-and-flavio-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">Brazilians voted Sunday in a high-stakes presidential election pitting incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva against far-right challenger Flavio Bolsonaro, following a campaign dominated by corruption scandals, economic anxiety and accusations of US meddling. The knife-edge election comes at a moment when the region is shifting to the right in line with the Trump administration.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Israel prepares to mark October 7</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9bfd03d24747376e121c0d2cf903fd5ed751f604c4a77305c993d8995da443f</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T10:59:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-prepares-to-mark-october-7--474582fa3044.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-prepares-to-mark-october-7" /><summary type="html">An Israeli strike on a civilian vehicle in Gaza on Sunday killed one Palestinian and wounded at least 11 others. Israel’s military said it was targeting a Hamas militant. Palestinians have reported a surge in Israeli fire and airstrikes across Gaza over the past month, with more than 75,000 people killed and much of the enclave destroyed. Meanwhile, Israelis held their weekly protest in Tel Aviv’s Hostages Square, the last before Wednesday marks three years since the October 7 attack. Protesters said they wanted to commemorate the victims and demand an independent state inquiry into the events and decisions that led to the attack. The Hamas-led assault killed around 1,200 people in Israel and saw more than 250 others taken hostage, according to Israeli authorities. Rachael Goldberg Polin, an American-Israeli activist and mother of slain hostage Hersh Goldberg-Polin, speaks to France 24.</summary></entry></feed>
